 ## Background
-Inverse Opacity Calculation, often referred to as Reparameterized Volume Sampling (RVS), was introduced by Khrulkhov et al. in 2023 [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the concept of inverse transform sampling used in NeRF but derives the sampling distribution from the density field directly rather than from a separate proposal network with auxiliary losses. The method leverages the mathematical equivalence between the CDF of the rendering contribution and the transmittance function [S2]. It is used in novel view synthesis and neural radiance field optimization [S1, unofficial].
